# Files Vercel must NOT upload, PLUS the package.json "main" rule (see below).
# Lesson 1 (14 Nov 2026, 100% error rate): with server.js uploaded, Vercel
# detected it as the root entrypoint ("Using server.js as the root
# entrypoint") and served ALL traffic through it as server.cjs — but
# server.js is the long-running PC process (listen() at load, exports
# { server }), so every invocation died with "Invalid export found in
# module /var/task/server.cjs".
# Lesson 2 (14 Nov 2026, build failed in 6s): excluding server.js via
# .vercelignore ALONE is not enough — package.json "main": "server.js"
# made Vercel look for that file as the entrypoint and fail the build
# with "No entrypoint found". package.json must NOT set "main" to
# server.js; with no "main" and no server file uploaded, Vercel builds
# api/index.js as a Serverless Function via file-system routing.
# The PC flow is unaffected: .vercelignore only affects Vercel uploads,
# git still tracks these files and `npm start` still runs server.js.
server.js
seen.js
test.js
test-vercel.js
